Portions of this project are adapted from GPT Academic:

  Project: GPT Academic
  Repository: https://github.com/binary-husky/gpt_academic
  License: GNU General Public License version 3

Adapted components include LaTeX/arXiv processing ideas and implementation
patterns for source downloading, LaTeX project parsing, content splitting, and
translation result merging. The implementation has been substantially modified
for a Codex skill workflow.

This project also references and draws implementation inspiration from
kaixindelele/chinarxiv:

  Project: chinarxiv
  Repository: https://github.com/kaixindelele/chinarxiv
  License: No explicit license file or GitHub-detected license was identified
           in the repository root at the time this notice was written.

Because no explicit upstream license was identified for kaixindelele/chinarxiv,
all rights in that upstream project remain with its respective author(s). This
project records attribution for the referenced ideas and workflow inspiration;
do not copy upstream code from that repository into this project unless its
license status is clarified or permission is obtained.

Major modifications in this project include:

- Packaging the workflow as a Codex skill.
- Using local Codex/subagents for translation orchestration.
- Requiring translated .tex and PDF output.
- Adding bilingual side-by-side PDF generation.
- Adding output cleanup, qa_warnings.json, and translation_log.log.
- Adding local smoke tests, including optional PDF compilation validation.
- Updating translation contract, workflow, and documentation for local agent use.

